{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992960-need-help-designing-a-persistent-condition","id":992960,"title":"Need help designing a persistent condition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-25T08:31:06-07:00","id":992960,"title":"Need help designing a persistent condition","content":"Hi everyone.<br /> <br /> A friend of mine is gonna st a standard mortal game for Halloween and he want us to, essentially, play ourselves as character. <br /> <br /> So i need help to create a persistent condition that would represent my moderate to high attention deficit problem. <br /> So far, i'm thinking something with penalties on extended rolls but i'm bad at the mechanical stuff.<br /> <br /> Thank you in advance for you help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T08:49:49-07:00","id":992967,"title":"","content":"Maybe instead of a penalty, it reduces the maximum number of rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T09:25:48-07:00","id":992977,"title":"","content":"I suggest a cumulative penalty of -1 for each roll. I.e. first roll at -1, second roll at -2, third roll at -3, and so on.<br /> That is, if you want a condition to define that part of you. I'm personally in favour of roleplaying personality problems and disorders since they're usually heavily context dependent and it can feel a bit degrading having a part of your personality being reduced to a mechanical effect. But you can do it however you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:02:51-07:00","id":993054,"title":"","content":"Well, the Patient Merit allows you to make two additional rolls on extended actions beyond your Attribute + Skill maximum. I could see an ADHD Condition reducing your number of rolls on an extended action. Something like...<br /> <br /> <u>Attention Deficit (Persistent)</u><br /> Your character struggles with maintaining engagement with tasks for extended periods of time. When attempting an extended action, your maximum number of rolls is reduced by two. Whenever you fail a roll on an extended action, you may take the Hyperactive Condition instead of any other Condition.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> You are unable to complete an important task as a result of your inattention.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Your character's attention deficit is cured by mundane or magical means.<br /> <br /> <u>Hyperactive</u><br /> Your character suffers from an over abundance of undirected energy. She may be jittery or tense, and focusing on the same task for extended periods of time requires significant effort. You suffer a -3 penalty on any roll that does not involve a Physical Attribute or Skill, and each roll beyond the first in an extended action costs a point of Willpower.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Your character abandons a task in favor of finding a better outlet for her energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-25-2016, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:47:37-07:00","id":993080,"title":"","content":"Um, i didnt think at all about reducing the maximum number of rolls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992960-need-help-designing-a-persistent-condition?p=993054#post993054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u>Attention Deficit (Persistent)</u><br /> Your character struggles with maintaining engagement with tasks for extended periods of time. When attempting an extended action, your maximum number of rolls is reduced by two. Whenever you fail a roll on an extended action, you may take the Hyperactive Condition instead of any other Condition.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> You are unable to complete an important task as a result of your inattention.<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Your character's attention deficit is cured by mundane or magical means.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that would work quite well. thank you<br /> <br /> Would you say that -2 is a good benchmark when looking at the effect of a negative condition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T15:42:30-07:00","id":993138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/992960-need-help-designing-a-persistent-condition?p=993080#post993080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, i didnt think at all about reducing the maximum number of rolls.<br /> <br /> I think that would work quite well. thank you<br /> <br /> Would you say that -2 is a good benchmark when looking at the effect of a negative condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>-2 can be a good go-to, depending on what you're trying to accomplish with the Condition. Personally I'm not a huge fan of straight-up dice penalties, they're kind of boring. The thing to keep in mind when designing Conditions, positive or negative, is that they should encourage the player to have their character act in a way that is consistent with what the Condition represents. If the Condition would logically cause a character to take a particular course of action, just making that course of action the way to resolve the Condition might be enough. If it would present a consistent problem for the character, it should give a small penalty reflecting that problem (like the above-mentioned -2 penalty), and the resolution criteria should be whatever it takes to rid the character of that problem. Persistent Conditions usually fall into the later category and have especially difficult resolution criteria. They should give a Beat when the problem the Condition presents causes an otherwise avoidable setback for the character or for the group. Mage has a great section on advice for designing Conditions and Tilts, I'd definitely recommend checking that out if you're interested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T21:40:14-07:00","id":993310,"title":"","content":"I have other request/proposition. For my one shot game I need <i>'Crisis of Faith' </i>Condition for protestant pastor character. I thought on something that each time she spends Willpower, she needs to spend two points - but I'm not sure here. Looking for some ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T04:33:08-07:00","id":993981,"title":"","content":"For both I would suggest a simplification already built-in the Condition rules.<br /> <br /> Instead of working hard on the actual numbers, just let the condition as a general guideline for roleplay. Whenever you find the opportunity, just call the Condition and do something &quot;stupid&quot; but in theme for it, or cease doing what you should do in the same fashion. You get the Beat, screw things a little (for the betterment of story, we hope), and feel how the Condition is actually playing out in the end.<br /> <br /> Maybe this experience data will let you make a better rule for the Condition when a longer game calls for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T06:42:13-07:00","id":994013,"title":"","content":"Yeah i see what you guys mean. Actually for condition what i think is that the beat generation and resolution rule seems to do more to help roleplay the condition than the modifiers it give (in my opinion, i've not yet experienced a lot of game with conditions). For the attention deficit i'd go that you gain a beat whenever you give up on a extended test instead of when you fail. I'd also give a beat for a temporary resolution when you take medicine (which have theyre own side effects, tho i dont intend to go that far for the game).<br /> <br /> I admit i was treating finding a condition for my attention deficit also partially as a thought experiment and i was curious to see in what way my attention deficit impacted on my life. (I'm very introspective so i like these opportunities).<br /> <br /> For the 'crisis of faith' instead of having willpower cost more dot, i would have that when you spend willpower you don't have the full 3 dice to roll maybe just 2 or 1. I'd see it as even though you can try very hard, in the end you don't really believe that you can succeed and thus it impact negatively on how hard you try.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T08:02:32-07:00","id":994025,"title":"","content":"For a crisis of faith, I would probably design it differently depending on the character and what their faith is. I would say they can't spend Willpower on certain rolls (which would vary depending on the details of the character's faith). If the character has Faithful as a Virtue, I'd also say they get a Beat any time they pass up an opportunity to regain Willpower from it. Otherwise, they'd just get a Beat when their lack of faith causes a setback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T00:18:21-08:00","id":1008844,"title":"","content":"Thinking on Crisis of Faith Condition - both 'stoping character from WP expenditure' and lowering WP bonus seems good idea. As it is for one-shot game I think that lower WP effect is more important, as chracters are to be thrown a lot of WP. So maybe chaning +3 bonus from WP into +2 and normal +2 into +1 is? For 'cannot make use WP situations' I would lend character a Beat then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T09:08:07-08:00","id":1008939,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that seems pretty reasonable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}